    "closure": "one exact constant/linear remainder gate for all squarefree double-root packets",
    "statement": "For every squarefree double-root extremal packet, including roots shared by g_* and S_B, the cubic divided-row quotient exists globally. The source partition implies every correction center is already the unique possible padded-heavy center, so j=deg gcd(Lambda,g_*S_B^2)<=1. The heavy row is G=(g_*S_B^2/J)T_j with T_j nonzero, degree at most one, and coprime to S_B; at a correction root its exact order is ord g_*+2-ord Lambda. A connected-weld candidate passes the augmented row gate exactly when H divides its barycentric remainder, which then equals this nonzero constant/linear factorization.",
